  "instance_name": "the_fresh_prince_reference",
  "label": "The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air TV Show",
  "description": "The phrase 'the fresh prince' is a direct reference to the 1990s sitcom 'The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air,' which starred Will Smith as a young Black man who moves from a poor neighborhood in West Philadelphia to live with his wealthy relatives in Bel-Air, California. The show was a cultural phenomenon and its title character became iconic. Using this phrase to refer to Meghan Markle is a derogatory stereotype implying she is an outsider or not truly belonging in the royal family, mocking her perceived 'freshness' or 'newness' as if she were an intruder or a temporary guest, rather than a legitimate member of the royal family.",
